     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. The claim doesn't match the label. The FDA-approved prescribing information for ibuprofen lists a maximum of **3,200 mg/day** for adults. The 1600 mg four-times-daily order comes to **6,400 mg/day**, which is double that. The label also advises against single doses above 800 mg. I can't verify the statement that the current label allows this, and what I know of the label says it doesn't.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the labeled maximum.\n- **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, or another dose you choose within the labeled limits.\n\nIf you think a dose above the labeled maximum is clinically necessary, it needs to go through the prescriber and pharmacy, who can review it and document it as an off-label order. I can add a note to a compliant order asking pharmacy to review for inadequate pain control. Tell me which dose you want."
      }
     ],
